  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>we know that by se the&nbsp;parallel axis theorem :-</p><p>Moment of inertia about a point which is parallel of the axis&nbsp;&nbsp;and at a distance of &nbsp;X&nbsp;given as&nbsp;</p><p><math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi></math> Parabola opening upward</p>"
